    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Architectural style",
      "items": [
        "This is closer to layered modular architecture than classic OO class architecture.",
        "Next.js Server Components own reads; Server Actions own mutations.",
        "Types define the domain contracts consumed across UI and data modules."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Boundaries to protect",
      "items": [
        "Pages and actions should keep going through @/lib/data, never direct Supabase.",
        "Storage logic belongs in data/documents.ts, not trips or pages.",
        "Dashboard authorization is split between middleware and server-side role guards.",
        "Public itinerary visibility is enforced by route logic plus database RLS assumptions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Local development fallback",
      "items": [
        "Most data modules branch on isSupabaseConfigured().",
        "Mock data lets the app run without Supabase, but should remain behind the data facade.",
        "Public itinerary visibility is enforced by route logic plus database RLS assumptions."
